{"assets":["/editorial-assets/4b6c0bffd47778a9723bf8c5884b924e6383801a8c859474dbea1793064a3bb0.png","/editorial-assets/82fc4b8446352e6cafbb144b123864fca6b2e6ab586b8166783934a4df7992f2.png","/editorial-assets/5454a1d56f76b5ba5685198c508083bf0d2d298b0dcf8e98332417436533174f.png","/editorial-assets/98616699c77f819c44f0f8df3b1191ee62394d955b213a943884c18429434d13.png","/editorial-assets/3bdc3a2620e2ea80f5159146abb8eb8882e542a5d6724ed11e3282e503c02637.png","/editorial-assets/69df199822f9eea89f8e5d449dd4af91a8eabda3e3bdfac611c9b9beb569892c.png","/editorial-assets/4d92916aa03a36904fdda60a17d960ec4f90db75cc70eba1f0aa8421a0ca3ed5.png","/editorial-assets/11c2b38ffc6675591510ca2324d69b09589ab872d6f17dc71d7e38a10c1c5a18.png","/editorial-assets/8e7e98b794b45e976f71fcdd1af7a477177be38634d1061933c9c400a88d0795.png","/editorial-assets/18cc6aa2fb5a5821c487baa2398d4e5e10cc7faffa1d2fb410447b773c2e3ac2.png","/editorial-assets/d31d5114bbcd84316b640de9d0f6fed1bc126415e1bb514f080e8957d80b4c21.png","/editorial-assets/7cc5d559f010bfc070912b8fd8d3a7b78fd66ebef32dcc63305e02f36cfbc1d8.png","/editorial-assets/7b2d9e465acc299ffda23882e3f42c2fda8847e7f8b82df7f9920e3938be2e2f.png","/editorial-assets/885de7c62b075ca144dab5e7231768e7358fbf116b827de189531cdab777138e.png","/editorial-assets/adb651167410ae10f13a39c1dec6ed07d4fc7b5ff8864ca61a1662917663ff05.png","/editorial-assets/af0d5d5c4eaa8f52cf568d5630a062faeff6922bbdcadf9f0e829483483b519f.png"],"contestId":"665","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/665/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"665A - Buses Between Cities"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem was suggested by Sergey Erlikh "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/unprost"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"unprost"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the time interval when Simion will be on the road strictly between cities ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 60"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"h"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Let's iterate over the oncoming buses. Let ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") be the time interval when the oncoming bus will be strictly between two cities. If the intersection of that intervals ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"max"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"), "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"min"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":")) is not empty than Simion will count that bus."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"С++ solution"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"int a, ta;\nint b, tb;\nint h, m;\n\nbool read() {\n\tif (!(cin >> a >> ta)) return false;\n\tassert(cin >> b >> tb);\n\tassert(scanf(\"%d:%d\", &h, &m) == 2);\n\treturn true;\n}\n\nvoid solve() {\n\tint x1 = h * 60 + m;\n\tint y1 = x1 + ta;\n\n\tint ans = 0;\n\tfor (int x2 = 5 * 60 + 0; x2 < 24 * 60; x2 += b) {\n\t\tint y2 = x2 + tb;\n\t\tint x = max(x1, x2), y = min(y1, y2);\n\t\tif (x < y)\n\t\t\tans++;\n\t}\n\tcout << ans << endl;\n}\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/665/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"665B - Shopping"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem was suggested by Ayush Anand "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/JeanValjean01"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"JeanValjean01"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem you should simply do what was written in the problem statement. There are no tricks."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"C++ solution"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"const int N = 111;\n\nint n, m, k;\nint p[N];\nint a[N][N];\n\nbool read() {\n\tif (!(cin >> n >> m >> k)) return false;\n\tforn(i, k) {\n\t\tassert(scanf(\"%d\", &p[i]) == 1);\n\t\tp[i]--;\n\t}\n\tforn(i, n)\n\t\tforn(j, m) {\n\t\t\tassert(scanf(\"%d\", &a[i][j]) == 1);\n\t\t\ta[i][j]--;\n\t\t}\n\treturn true;\n}\n\nvoid solve() {\n\tint ans = 0;\n\tforn(i, n)\n\t\tforn(j, m) {\n\t\t\tint pos = int(find(p, p + k, a[i][j]) - p);\n\t\t\tans += pos + 1;\n\t\t\tnfor(l, pos) p[l + 1] = p[l];\n\t\t\tp[0] = a[i][j];\n\t\t}\n\tcout << ans << endl;\n}\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nmk"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/665/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"665C - Simple Strings"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem was suggested by Zi Song Yeoh "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/zscoder"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"zscoder"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are two ways to solve this problem: greedy approach and dynamic programming."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first apprroach: Considerr some segment of consecutive equal characters. Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the length of that segment. Easy to see that we should change at least "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/4b6c0bffd47778a9723bf8c5884b924e6383801a8c859474dbea1793064a3bb0.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters in the segment to remove all the pairs of equal consecutive letters. On the other hand we can simply change the second, the fourth etc. symbols to letter that is not equal to the letters before and after the segment."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Greedy approach on C++"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"const int N = 200200;\n\nint n;\nchar s[N];\n\nbool read() {\n\tif (!gets(s)) return false;\n\tn = int(strlen(s));\n\treturn true;\n}\n\nvoid solve() {\n\tfor (int i = 0, j = 0; i < n; i = j) {\n\t\twhile (j < n && s[j] == s[i]) j++;\n\t\tchar c = 'a';\n\t\twhile (c == s[i] || (i > 0 && c == s[i - 1]) || (j < n && c == s[j]))\n\t\t\tc++;\n\t\tfore(k, i, j)\n\t\t\tif ((i + k) & 1)\n\t\t\t\ts[k] = c;\n\t}\n\tputs(s);\n}\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second approach: Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ka"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the minimal number of changes so that the prefix of length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" has no equal consecutive letters and the symbol "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"'"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let's iterate over the letter on the position "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 and if it is not equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" make transition. The cost of the transition is equal to 0 if we put the same letter as in the original string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" on the position "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1. Otherwise the cost is equal to 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"DP solution on C++"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"const int N = 1200300, A = 27;\n\nint n;\nchar s[N];\n\nbool read() {\n\tif (!gets(s)) return false;\n\tn = int(strlen(s));\n\treturn true;\n}\n\nint z[N][A];\nint p[N][A];\nchar ans[N];\n\nvoid solve() {\n\tmemset(z, 63, sizeof(z));\n\n\tz[0][A - 1] = 0;\n\tforn(i, n) {\n\t\tint c = int(s[i] - 'a');\n\t\tforn(j, A) {\n\t\t\tint dv = z[i][j];\n\t\t\tif (dv > INF / 2) continue;\n\t\t\tforn(nj, A - 1) {\n\t\t\t\tif (nj == j) continue;\n\t\t\t\tint ct = nj != c;\n\t\t\t\tif (z[i + 1][nj] > dv + ct) {\n\t\t\t\t\tz[i + 1][nj] = dv + ct;\n\t\t\t\t\tp[i + 1][nj] = j;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tint idx = int(min_element(z[n], z[n] + A) - z[n]);\n\n\tfor (int i = n, j = idx; i > 0; j = p[i][j], i--)\n\t\tans[i - 1] = char('a' + j);\n\tans[n] = 0;\n\n\tcerr << z[n][idx] << endl;\n\tputs(ans);\n}\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/665/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"665D - Simple Subset"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem was suggested by Zi Song Yeoh "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/zscoder"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"zscoder"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the subset "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" that is the answer to the problem. Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the arbitrary three elements from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and let no more than one of them is equal to 1. By the pigeonhole principle two of three elements from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" have the same parity. So we have two integers with even sum and only one of them is equal to 1, so their sum is also greater than 2. So the subset "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is not simple. In this way "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" consists of only two numbers greater than one (with a prime sum) or consists of some number of ones and also maybe other value "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", so that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 is a prime."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We can simply process the first case in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") time. The second case can be processed in linear time. Also we should choose the best answer from that two."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To check the value of order 2·10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"6"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" for primality in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1) time we can use the simple or the linear Eratosthenes sieve."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"C++ solution"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"const int N = 1010, X = 2100300;\n\nint n, a[N];\n\nbool read() {\n\tif (!(cin >> n)) return false;\n\tforn(i, n) assert(scanf(\"%d\", &a[i]) == 1);\n\treturn true;\n}\n\nint szp, p[X];\nint mind[X];\n\nvoid prepare() {\n\tfore(i, 2, X) {\n\t\tif (!mind[i]) {\n\t\t\tp[szp++] = i;\n\t\t\tmind[i] = i;\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < szp && p[j] <= mind[i] && i * p[j] < X; j++)\n\t\t\tmind[i * p[j]] = p[j];\n\t}\n}\n\nvoid printAns(int cnt1, int a = -1, int b = -1) {\n\tvector<int> ans;\n\tforn(i, cnt1) ans.pb(1);\n\tif (a != -1) ans.pb(a);\n\tif (b != -1) ans.pb(b);\n\tassert(!ans.empty());\n\trandom_shuffle(all(ans));\n\n\tcout << sz(ans) << endl;\n\tforn(i, sz(ans)) {\n\t\tif (i) putchar(' ');\n\t\tprintf(\"%d\", ans[i]);\n\t}\n\tputs(\"\");\n}\n\nvoid solve() {\n\tint cnt1 = (int) count(a, a + n, 1);\n\n\tfunction<bool(int)> isPrime = [](int p) { return mind[p] == p; };\n\n\tif (cnt1 > 0)\n\t\tforn(i, n)\n\t\t\tif (a[i] != 1 && isPrime(a[i] + 1)) {\n\t\t\t\tprintAns(cnt1, a[i]);\n\t\t\t\treturn;\n\t\t\t}\n\n\tif (cnt1 > 1) {\n\t\tprintAns(cnt1);\n\t\treturn;\n\t}\n\n\tforn(i, n)\n\t\tforn(j, i)\n\t\t\tif (isPrime(a[i] + a[j])) {\n\t\t\t\tprintAns(0, a[i], a[j]);\n\t\t\t\treturn;\n\t\t\t}\n\n\tprintAns(0, a[0]);\n}\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the maximal value in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/665/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"665E - Beautiful Subarrays"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem was suggested by Zi Song Yeoh "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/zscoder"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"zscoder"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The sign "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/82fc4b8446352e6cafbb144b123864fca6b2e6ab586b8166783934a4df7992f2.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" is used for the binary operation for bitwise exclusive or."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the xor of the first "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" elements on the prefix of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then the interval ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] is beautiful if "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/5454a1d56f76b5ba5685198c508083bf0d2d298b0dcf8e98332417436533174f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let's iterate over "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" from 1 to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and consider the values "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" as the binary strings. On each iteration we should increase the answer by the value "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of numbers "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") so "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/5454a1d56f76b5ba5685198c508083bf0d2d298b0dcf8e98332417436533174f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". To do that we can use the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trie"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"trie"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" data structure. Let's store in the trie all the values "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Besides the structure of the trie we should also store in each vertex the number of leaves in the subtree of that vertex (it can be easily done during adding of each binary string). To calculate the value "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" let's go down by the trie from the root. Let's accumulate the value "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cur"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals to the xor of the prefix of the value "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" with the already passed in the trie path. Let the current bit in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the depth of the current vertex in the trie. If the number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cur"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≥ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" then we can increase "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" by the number of leaves in vertex "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/98616699c77f819c44f0f8df3b1191ee62394d955b213a943884c18429434d13.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", because all the leaves in the subtree of tha vertex correspond to the values "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" that for sure gives "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/5454a1d56f76b5ba5685198c508083bf0d2d298b0dcf8e98332417436533174f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". After that we should go down in the subtree "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Otherwise 